%C - read or write physical (device) memory

Syntax:
%C [-w width] address [count]          read
%C [-w width] address = value          write

   -w width   access width in bytes: 1, 2, 4 (default) or 8
   address, count and value accept 0x prefixes

Examples:
   %C 0x1f00200000 4        four 32-bit words from the first RP1 xHCI
   %C 0x1000124068          PCIe2 root complex status
WARNING: an access to an address nothing answers on can crash the system.
